intention:
  name: "The Hive's screen in tags with qs: (Quantum OS)"
  version: "1.0.0"
  category: "screen"
  goal: |
    Let a person declare, in one file, what the Hive of Quantum OS shows on
    the machine's screen and what happens in it when something happens on
    the system, and get the scene a small daemon draws on the console with
    no engine and no GPU, every promise in the file checked before it runs.

  principles:
    - "One schema (quantum/runtime/screen/schema.py) is the language: a tag, an attribute, an event or an action it does not list is a compile error naming the line"
    - "Declarations only: there are no statements and no expressions; text where a tag goes is refused ('a screen file is declarations, not script')"
    - "A {field} is a field of the event the rule is on, filled in by hive-screen from the event itself; in the scene it is refused, because the scene is fixed"
    - "A sprite's name is how a rule reaches it: a target that is a {field} finds the sprite of that name, or nothing happens"
    - "The scene's vocabulary is the games': qs:sheet, qs:animation, qs:sprite, qs:tween with the same trans and ease, qs:particles with the same presets, qs:emit, qs:emitter"
    - "Approving is never declared: qs:offers is built in, with the dashboard's semantics, and hive-cortex decides who may"
    - "A frame is the same on every machine: what a test compares is pixels in the daemon's own test, and data (what the screen shows) everywhere else"

  capabilities:
    - "Declare the sheets (qs:sheet, qs:animation) and the effects (qs:particles) a screen uses"
    - "Lay out the scene (qs:scene): qs:sprite, qs:text, qs:emitter, the built-in qs:offers and qs:notices"
    - "Per event (qs:on): qs:animate, qs:frame, qs:show, qs:tween, qs:emit, qs:say, with {field}s of the event"
    - "React to every observation the rules know: service-crash, log-anomaly, port-conflict, disk-low, memory-pressure, command-observed, command-not-found"
    - "React to the screen's own events: notice, offer, done, failed"

  triggers:
    - '<q:application type="screen">'
    - "qs:scene"
    - "qs:sprite"
    - "qs:on"
    - "the Hive's screen, what the Hive shows, the console, pixel art for Quantum OS"

  structure: |
    <q:application id="screen" type="screen">
      qs:sheet name= src= tile=          a PNG of frames
        qs:animation name= frames= fps= loop=
      qs:particles name= preset= ...     an effect
      qs:scene width= height= background=
        qs:sprite name= sheet= frame= x= y= animation= hidden=
        qs:text value= x= y= color= align=
        qs:emitter particles= x= y= width= level=
        qs:offers x= y= width= rows=     the Hive's offers, built in
        qs:notices x= y= width= rows=    the last notices, built in
      qs:on event="..."                  one rule per event
        qs:animate / qs:frame / qs:show / qs:tween / qs:emit / qs:say
    </q:application>
